# Example 27: DNA storage codec benchmark (S5)
# A scenario-decision tool: which DNA storage codec for which data
# scenario?  The codecs are benchmarked at fixed code rates (0.5 / 1.0 /
# 1.5 bit/nt) by scanning how much sequence loss and per-base error each
# can tolerate before the payload becomes unrecoverable, together with
# the per-GB cost (2024 synthesis/sequencing prices) and decode time.
#
# Expected trade-off (Erlich & Zielinski 2017, Science 355:950):
#   - fountain: as the code rate falls, tolerated molecule loss rises
#     (~0.5 bit/nt survives > 60% loss; the near-native rate survives
#     almost none).
#   - rs (block Reed-Solomon): the mirror image - it corrects base
#     errors (more redundancy at low density), but losing any whole
#     block is irrecoverable.
#   - goldman: fixed native density (built-in 4x overlap), no rate knob.
#
# The robustness scan runs through the #sim extension point
# (kind=codec_benchmark) using helixlang.plugins.apps.dna_storage.benchmark_codecs;
# the #gene below is the payload being stored.

#gene name=storage_payload
ATG GCT GGT GTA TAA
#end

#config backend=fba ticks=1
#sim kind=codec_benchmark densities=0.5,1.0,1.5 data_size=256 seed=7
#sim output=scheme,target_density,max_loss_fraction,max_error_rate,cost_per_gb_usd
